# Frozen 2026-11-11 from redis-memtier/pilot/ (pilot_report.txt; README timeline 53).
# Doubling ladder, 8x span, the same shape as nginx's (5k/10k/20k/40k) and
# fio's, so level k sits at the same fraction of each workload's top rate.
# Topped at 40000 req/s, about 74 % of the untraced plateau (about 53900
# req/s from 100000 up). The plateau is redis's single command thread
# (redis CPU 1.00 core); memtier used at most 1.26 of its 2 cores. 50000 was
# reached untraced (49908) but p99 had already doubled (1.67 -> 3.14 ms), and
# tracing takes CPU from that one redis core, so 50000 was left as headroom.
# Every rate is a multiple of 2500 (memtier's 20 ms refill). 5000 and 40000
# were not pilot points; the smoke cell is their first check. Changing any
# line means a new results directory: schema.json records the ladder.
LADDER="1:5000 2:10000 3:20000 4:40000"
MEMTIER_THREADS=2
MEMTIER_CLIENTS=25
